      },
      "supports": "Given a comparison algorithm for the coordinate-or-absence output, simulate each comparison by reading at most two values. On a coordinate output, use at most one additional read to recover the alleged saddlepoint value. A correct output gives the correct decision and value. Therefore the randomized entry-read lower bound in Theorem 15 at success probability 5/6 also bounds worst-instance expected comparison cost up to a constant factor and one read.",
